  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nUpper ridging over the western U.S. will remain the dominant force\nthis weekend with triple digit heat during the afternoon hours\ntoday and Sunday. Low temperatures tonight will struggle to get\ndown to the mid 60s to mid 70s, making for uncomfortable sleeping\nconditions for those without air conditioning. Will continue the\nExtreme Heat Warning through 10pm Sunday evening. \n\nThere will be enough instability with a shortwave trough\napproaching from the southwest this afternoon and evening to\ninitiate a few dry thunderstorms. HREF max ensemble wind gust\nguidance continues to support the potential for damaging wind\ngusts as a primary threat, further noting the inverted-v forecast\nsoundings across the area. A Red Flag Warning for fire zones 134,\n135, 136, and 137 continues for this afternoon due to the\nlightning risk on dry fuels. As an aside, haze and some smoke will\ncontinue at times to be a problem from upstream wildfires.\n\nEnsembles continue to show the hot temperatures continuing through\nat least the early and middle part of next week, with highs in the\n90s to around 100 degrees each day.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nPops were adjusted for consistency and collaboration with\nneighbors in support of near term high resolution guidance. There\nis above average confidence for hot temperatures through the\nbalance of the weekend and into the first part of next week, with\nonly some uncertainty due to impact from smoke and haze.\nConfidence is above average for isolated convective coverage at\nleast this evening, though lower for specific timing and\nplacement.",
